{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "target" or render_mode == "interject_inline" or render_mode == "short_inline" %}
{# render_mode guard MUST be within the first 5 lines (see 0330). #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{# Relationships - the officiant (2.5, Build A; spec 5.3, 5.4)                  #}
{#                                                                            #}
{# Any priest, priestess or jarl can marry the player to their betrothed,      #}
{# here and now, unplanned. Officiants are seldom enrolled, so 0330 never       #}
{# reaches them: this tells them only when it matters - someone engaged to the #}
{# player is here with them. Silent otherwise. get_officiant is native.        #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% if not is_player(actorUUID) %}
{% if is_plugin_loaded("SNRom_Integration.esl") or is_plugin_loaded("SNRom_Integration.esp") %}
{% if render_mode == "interject_inline" or render_mode == "short_inline" %}
{# WHOSE TURN IT IS, FOR SKYRIMNET'S CHOICE OF SPEAKER (wpm77; the author,
   2026-10-31: "prevent her from skipping steps"). SkyrimNet picks who speaks
   next from each candidate's interject_inline, and whom the player is
   talking to from their short_inline; nothing can forbid a pick, but these
   say whose turn it is in the wedding under way, for everyone near: the
   officiant and the betrothed speak in their turn, guests not at all. The
   DLL's cues need no pick (DirectNarration names its speaker). Here, not in
   0330, because the guests have no bond to render. Silent with no wedding. #}
{% set wt = get_wedding_turn(actorUUID) %}
{% if default(wt.wedding, 0) == 1 %}
{% set me = decnpc(actorUUID).name %}
{% set whose = "" %}
{% if wt.turn == "officiant" %}{% set whose = wt.officiant %}{% elif wt.turn == "player" %}{% set whose = player.name %}{% elif wt.turn == "betrothed" %}{% set whose = wt.betrothed %}{% endif %}
{% if render_mode == "interject_inline" %}
{% if wt.role == "guest" %}
A wedding is under way here: {{ wt.officiant }} is marrying {{ player.name }} and {{ wt.betrothed }}. {{ me }} watches in silence and does not interject, unless spoken to by name.
{% else %}
Right now {{ me }} is {% if wt.role == "officiant" %}marrying {{ player.name }} and {{ wt.betrothed }}{% else %}being married to {{ player.name }}{% endif %}{% if wt.turn == wt.role %}, and it is {{ me }}'s turn to speak.{% elif whose != "" %}; it is {{ whose }}'s turn, not {{ me }}'s, so {{ me }} does not interject, and speaks only when called on in the wedding.{% else %}; {{ me }} waits in silence for the wedding to go on, and does not interject.{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% elif wt.role == "officiant" %}
Marrying {{ player.name }} and {{ wt.betrothed }}, now{% if wt.step == 5 or wt.step == 6 %}: {{ me }} has asked {{ player.name }} whether they take {{ wt.betrothed }}, so what {{ player.name }} says now is their answer to {{ me }}{% endif %}.
{% elif wt.role == "betrothed" %}
Being married to {{ player.name }}, now{% if wt.step == 1 or wt.step == 2 %}: {{ player.name }}'s vows, when they speak them, are for {{ me }}{% elif wt.step == 5 or wt.step == 6 %}: what {{ player.name }} says now is their answer to {{ wt.officiant }}, not to {{ me }}{% endif %}.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
{% set off = get_officiant(actorUUID) %}
{# THE WEDDING YOU ARE CONDUCTING (Ceremony.h), by step, the minimum for any
   ceremony (the author, 2026-10-20): 1 open and ask for the player's vows,
   2 the player's vows, 3 the betrothed's vows, 4 ask the player "do you
   take", 5 their answer, 6 ask the betrothed, 7 their answer, 8 pronounce
   them married. Vows come BEFORE the questions (wpm17 asked for vows after,
   and the betrothed answered the question twice). The DLL moves the steps on
   when it hears each line; this says what this step is, so the words fit. #}
{% if off and default(off.officiant, 0) == 1 and default(off.ceremony, 0) > 0 %}
{% set them = default(off.marrying, "your betrothed") %}
{% set step = off.ceremony %}

## The Wedding You Are Conducting

You are marrying {{ player.name }} and {{ them }}, now, here, before whoever is present. It is a wedding, not a chat: speak as one who marries people, with the solemnity and warmth that are yours. It goes in this order: {% if default(off.planned, 0) == 1 %}the wedding they planned, so first your words to everyone gathered and anything else they chose, then {% endif %}your opening, {{ player.name }}'s vows, {{ them }}'s vows, then you ask each of them in turn whether they take the other, {% if default(off.rings, 0) == 1 %}then they exchange rings, {% endif %}then you pronounce them married{% if default(off.kiss, 0) == 1 %} and invite them to kiss, and once they have, you present them to everyone, married{% endif %}. One step at a time; never run ahead. No one is married until both have answered you.
{# How to answer this step is said at the end of the prompt since wpm88: user_final_instructions/8100_relationships_actions. #}
{% else %}
{% if off and default(off.officiant, 0) == 1 and existsIn(off, "weddings") and length(off.weddings) > 0 %}

## Weddings You Have Agreed To

{# STOPPED SHORT (the author, 2026-10-31, wpm67): a wedding that went no
   further, or met a no, does not begin again by itself. The officiant may
   offer, and MarriageBless begins the planned wedding again. #}
{% for w in off.weddings %}- {{ player.name }} and {{ w.betrothed }}{% if w.day != "" %}, {{ w.day }}{% endif %}{% if w.place != "" %}, at {{ w.place }}{% endif %}{% if default(w.stoppedShort, 0) == 1 %}: today. You began it, but it went no further, and it will not begin again on its own. When you are with them, you may offer to begin again from the start; if they want to, begin it, as you would to marry them here and now{% elif default(w.underWay, 0) == 1 %}: today; be there{% endif %}.
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if off and default(off.officiant, 0) == 1 and default(off.ceremony, 0) == 0 and existsIn(off, "betrothed") and length(off.betrothed) > 0 %}

## Who Has Come Before You

{# NO LOOP VARIABLE CALLED "name" (seen in play, wpm56): inja leaves a loop's
   variable behind, emptied, after the loop; "name" left so broke SkyrimNet's
   render of the whole profile (SEH, read at 0x18) - the officiant saw only
   her summary. join() needs no variable. #}
{{ player.name }} is here with {{ join(off.betrothed, " and ") }}, to whom they are engaged. As one who can marry people, you could marry them here and now, if they ask you and you are willing: a few words fitting the moment, then you ask each of them in turn whether they take the other, and when both have said yes, you pronounce them married. Whether you would is yours to judge, as yourself. Or, if they would rather a wedding on a day of their own choosing, you may agree to marry them then, at the place they choose.
{% if default(off.mayMarry, 1) == 0 %}
But {{ player.name }} is already married, and Mara has granted them no exception. You know it, and you will not marry them to another. Say so in your own way.
{% elif default(off.exception, 0) == 1 and default(off.spouses, 0) > 0 %}
{{ player.name }} holds Mara's own exception to marry more than once. Every priest knows it; you may still have an opinion.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
